RC3 is a top-secret research installation of the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]], buried under an unmarked office building in [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/Sarengrad|Sarengrad]]. Its front is a reception room labelled the Office for Regional Logistics, with a desk, potted plants and shelves of generic set-piece books; past it there are no offices at all, only a locked door with a small pad beside it. Entry runs the House's usual path: a passcard of any tier, a soul print, the fall of water called the Liar's Downfall, and an elevator down. A card opens only the floors at its own tier. The tiers run red, orange, yellow, green, blue, violet and ultraviolet, and the few ultraviolet cards open the whole facility. [[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]] holds one.

The floors grow stranger the deeper they go. On the first, red tier the Paranectural Cartography Division lies to the left of the elevator and the Department of Dimensional Correspondence to the right, a mail room of pneumatic tubing where five people hang fifteen feet in the air, mouths open and yellow light spilling out, all speaking the same words together. The Office of Symbiotic Interactions and the Bureau of Emotional Contagion lie between. The Bureau of Emotional Contagion is a gallery of abstract paintings, each one tied to an emotion. Signs warn that this is a deja vu area, and that anyone who feels they have been there before is to report to a superior at once.

The second, orange tier holds the Bureau of Linguistic Aberrations to the left, its floors heaped with pages of mad ramblings kept in case a madman proved a true oracle, and the Department of Ontological Stability to the right, a plain concrete cube with a terminal and a painted circle ringed by lamps, a small [[Phenomena/Althane/Ontological Anchor|ontological anchor]] turning above the middle of the circle. At the end of that hallway sits a doorway marked Firebreak Alpha, and behind it there is only empty void where the firebreak should be.

The third, yellow tier holds the Department of Recursive Entities to the left and the Office of Mnemonic Preservation to the right. Recursive Entities is drafting tables and a door set with two rows of labelled dials. The Office of Mnemonic Preservation keeps the memory of the facility: shelves of small white spools of thread, each with its own coded plaque, played back on a loom-like headset called a Speely. Further down the same hallway lie the Threshold Expeditions Office and Firebreak Beta, and a sign beneath them points on to Beacon Containment on the fifth floor.

Threshold Expeditions is a concrete cube that holds four freestanding stone doorways, each with a lamp cord and a nine-digit keypad whose Oreskian symbols reorder themselves whenever someone steps away. A code of twenty-eight characters opens one, and a door leads somewhere else entirely. Firebreak Beta opens on a black void, with a black stone platform and a keycard scanner jutting from it and another opening some eight hundred feet away. The Blacklight Initiative lies along the same corridor: a dark room of pillars and black orbs of lightning that hang over specially built altars and snare whoever passes, holding them stunned while the bolts fall.

The sixth floor holds the Eschatology division behind the cognitive breakwater. It stood empty and mid-crisis when the [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|Deep]] broke through: a klaxon sounded every few seconds and a voice in Oreskian repeated its warnings, of a cognitive breakwater on the sixth floor, threshold manifestations on every floor, an unplanned architectural restructure in progress, and Contingency A12 in force to hold off a mnemonic breach. Hallways and ceilings rearranged themselves as they were walked, and the air carried a static at the back of the mind. Surviving personnel were called to Firebreak Gamma on the fifth floor, and the facility was sealed against any exit. Where the Deep has reached, people rise off the floor into the air, mouths and eyes spilling yellow light, and speak with one voice. [[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]] declared the breakwater resolved and lifted the lockdown, and it was here that he was killed, the [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|Deep]] reaching through a portal to take his body.

The sixth floor's doors are labelled from the elevator: to the left the eschatology division, the vault, and the residences, all behind ultraviolet; to the right a single door to beacon maintenance and main storage, behind violet. It is the last floor; there is no seventh.

The residences lie behind an automatic door that opens for someone it senses. Beyond it is a dome about three hundred feet across, floored with grass under a projected sky that loops, and three small houses of one shape stand in it. The three who ran the installation slept here, [[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]], [[People/Althane/Natalia|Natalia]] and [[People/Althane/Rampart|Rampart]]. Karkov's house is the plainest, a bed, a desk, a window on a meadow and an empty weapon rack, and a locket kept in the desk holds portraits of Rampart and [[People/Althane/The Slipseer|the Slipseer]] as children.

Beacon maintenance and main storage is bright where the rest of the facility is bare concrete: its floor, walls and ceiling are set with glass in many colours, and raised platforms stand about the room with a long gantry above. Rings lie set into the floor, like doorways that open on nothing. In the centre a great spool hangs from cables, turning on its own axis and circling the room at once, with cords appearing out of the air and winding onto it; the cords are stored minds, drawn from the dead and wound away on the spool. Against the far wall stand three glass tubes fifteen feet tall; the [[Bestiary/Kaathe|Kaathe]] [[People/Althane/Halidex Op-B|Hali]] and [[People/Althane/Tennobrin Er-K|Tenno]] floated in two of them, one giving off faint red light and one faint blue, and the third stood empty. Main storage has since been wrecked, its tubes broken and the minds it kept destroyed.
